  "stepTexts": [
   "Slice the 1½ lb flank steak against the grain into ¼-inch strips, then toss with ¼ teaspoon baking soda, 2 tablespoons soy sauce, 1 tablespoon cornstarch, and ½ tablespoon sesame oil; let sit 15 minutes to velvet.",
   "Core, seed, and cut the 2 green bell peppers and 1 red bell pepper into 1-inch pieces; halve and slice the yellow onion into half-moons; mince the 4 garlic cloves; peel and finely grate 1 teaspoon fresh ginger.",
   "Whisk together ¾ cup beef broth, 2 tablespoons oyster sauce, 1 tablespoon hoisin sauce, 1 tablespoon Shaoxing rice wine, 1 tablespoon dark soy sauce, 1 teaspoon sugar, and ¾ teaspoon coarsely ground black pepper in a small bowl; in a separate small bowl, dissolve 2 tablespoons cornstarch in 2 tablespoons water to make a slurry.",
   "Heat 2 tablespoons neutral oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat until shimmering, then add the marinated beef in a single layer and sear undisturbed for 1 minute; stir-fry for 1 more minute until just browned but not fully cooked through, then transfer to a plate.",
   "Add the remaining 1 tablespoon neutral oil to the wok over high heat, add the onion and stir-fry for 2 minutes until slightly softened, then add the bell peppers and stir-fry for 2 more minutes until crisp-tender.",
   "Push the vegetables to the edges of the wok, add the garlic and ginger to the center, and stir-fry for 30 seconds until fragrant.",
   "Pour the brown sauce mixture into the wok and bring to a boil, stirring to combine with the vegetables, then stir in the cornstarch slurry and cook for 1 minute until the sauce is glossy and thickened.",
   "Return the seared beef and any resting juices to the wok, toss everything together over high heat for 1 minute until the beef is cooked through and fully coated in the sauce, then drizzle with the remaining ½ tablespoon sesame oil.",
   "Transfer to a serving platter and serve immediately over steamed jasmine rice."
  ],
